Observable repository
In the previous example, the responsibility of choosing between the remote data and the
local data fell onto the view model. If we could actually notify the view-model about the
changing result (that is, local and remote data), we would need to pass the local repository
instance to the view-model. By using reactive extensions, we could implement a notifying
observable and subscribe to various events on the view-model:
OnNext: We would update the data within the view model, which would be
fired twice
OnCompleted: We would hide any progress indicator we have been showing up
until this point
